02:10:43.630 --> 02:10:46.910
lack of understanding. So can you explain, like, is 20 litres

02:10:47.410 --> 02:10:51.470
per second enough for one household on average or like

02:10:51.970 --> 02:10:55.270
high rise? Like, what is that through the chair?

02:10:55.770 --> 02:10:58.550
I may have to defer to Ryan if he's still here, because I don't know

02:10:59.050 --> 02:11:02.320
if you have those numbers. I don't at my fingertips to know what. One litre

02:11:02.820 --> 02:11:05.720
per second equates to, and I realise you're talking about averages, like we can,

02:11:06.220 --> 02:11:10.120
yeah, but help me through the

02:11:10.620 --> 02:11:14.760
chair. So the average water demand changes year over year as we recalculate

02:11:15.260 --> 02:11:19.240
our numbers, but we're generally around 355 people for

02:11:19.740 --> 02:11:23.600
every one litre per second. 355 people,

02:11:24.100 --> 02:11:27.360
one litre per second times 20,

02:11:27.900 --> 02:11:32.060
Equals what? Or like...

02:11:32.560 --> 02:11:35.580
Quick math. I would need to pull out a calculator.

02:11:37.500 --> 02:11:48.460
Somebody's working their calculator, hang on. I mean, I could too, but through

02:11:48.960 --> 02:11:52.940
the chair, 7100. Okay, this is... That is good

02:11:53.440 --> 02:11:57.100
news, right? Okay, thank you.

02:11:58.940 --> 02:12:03.100
Councillor Vrbanovic. Thank you very much

02:12:03.600 --> 02:12:08.380
and lots of good questions and discussion. I just wanted to follow

02:12:08.880 --> 02:12:12.660
up on this resiliency piece and I think, you know,

02:12:13.160 --> 02:12:16.300
as has been explained and always important to remind ourselves,

02:12:16.460 --> 02:12:19.880
there's really two issues we're dealing with. One is an infrastructure

02:12:21.550 --> 02:12:25.550
and the other one is looking at the broader

02:12:26.050 --> 02:12:29.790
issue of our aquifers and so on, and the

02:12:29.870 --> 02:12:33.430
capacity of getting the

02:12:33.930 --> 02:12:37.550
water that we need, and work is happening on both of those spaces.

02:12:38.030 --> 02:12:41.350
But I guess I just want to really

02:12:41.850 --> 02:12:44.350
understand, and Ken, maybe this is a question for you,

02:12:46.270 --> 02:12:49.900
