02:12:59.400 --> 02:13:02.820
the fullness of time. Some say it's

02:13:03.320 --> 02:13:05.420
the right number because we're on an aquifer based system.

02:13:06.940 --> 02:13:11.540
You know, you've come at it with a fresh set

02:13:12.040 --> 02:13:15.540
of eyes. Is it the right number? Do we

02:13:16.040 --> 02:13:17.980
not know if it's the right number at the present time?

02:13:19.250 --> 02:13:22.850
I get that right now while we're waiting for some of our infrastructure improvements

02:13:23.350 --> 02:13:26.530
to happen, maybe it needs to be the right number,

02:13:26.770 --> 02:13:29.250
but is it the right number in the longer term?

02:13:32.770 --> 02:13:36.410
Thank you for the question. I think we

02:13:36.910 --> 02:13:40.770
have to cast back to the comments that Director

02:13:41.270 --> 02:13:44.530
Shaw had talked about, is that currently we're operating in the negative.

02:13:45.980 --> 02:13:49.220
And if you kind of look at the puts and the takes in terms of

02:13:49.720 --> 02:13:51.340
things that are offline and where the demands are,

02:13:53.660 --> 02:13:56.860
so we need the 20% now because in fact

02:13:57.420 --> 02:14:01.780
we're kind of exceeding that reserve

02:14:02.280 --> 02:14:05.500
headroom capacity. It's acute

02:14:06.000 --> 02:14:08.820
in our system because of the complexity of the wells that we have and we're

02:14:09.320 --> 02:14:12.460
vulnerable with this well source of supply. That's just what it is.

02:14:13.520 --> 02:14:17.480
So as I come in and look at this scenario, it's very different than

02:14:17.980 --> 02:14:21.760
virtually every other system that I've worked in. The sensitivity to the well systems

02:14:22.260 --> 02:14:25.800
here, as opposed to a surface water supply where you have a single treatment plant

02:14:26.300 --> 02:14:32.320
or multiple treatment plants, we have 50. And so

02:14:32.820 --> 02:14:36.360
we have to be very cautious in that we're vulnerable

02:14:36.860 --> 02:14:40.680
in terms of the aquifer restrictions that we're facing

02:14:41.180 --> 02:14:44.300
now compared to a source supply system where you can

02:14:44.800 --> 02:14:48.700
simply draft from the lake that you effectively have an infinite supply in

02:14:49.200 --> 02:14:52.980
many jurisdictions. So we're doing the analysis now and I know

02:14:53.620 --> 02:14:57.260
we'd all like to have this information tomorrow but we need to do the risk-based

02:14:57.760 --> 02:15:01.580
assessment where this is going to come back. As Nicole

02:15:02.080 --> 02:15:05.780
had mentioned earlier, this will come up in terms of is that the right number,

