02:38:15.070 --> 02:38:18.870
knowing that in the horizon this was going to come up. And that's what

02:38:19.370 --> 02:38:22.830
this motion is all about. It's all about how did we get

02:38:23.330 --> 02:38:27.790
here and understanding how we got here and how we're going to make recommendations

02:38:28.270 --> 02:38:31.670
to make sure it doesn't happen again. And that's what the

02:38:32.170 --> 02:38:35.870
motion is really all about. So I'm going

02:38:36.370 --> 02:38:40.520
to read to you, I don't like reading to people, but forgive

02:38:47.680 --> 02:38:51.600
Okay, so there's a number of things I wanted

02:38:52.100 --> 02:38:55.360
to say about this motion. Why we need to review, I want to talk about

02:38:55.860 --> 02:38:59.800
staff workload because the pushback I'm getting is staff can't

02:39:00.300 --> 02:39:03.640
handle these kind of things of an inquiry and so

02:39:04.140 --> 02:39:07.540
on. I want to talk to you quickly too about whether

02:39:08.040 --> 02:39:11.660
this is precedent setting and also the consequences of not

02:39:12.160 --> 02:39:15.660
doing it. So I'm giving you a brief update about where I'm heading.

02:39:16.380 --> 02:39:20.540
The water capacity crisis affecting the region of Waterloo

02:39:20.780 --> 02:39:23.340
has serious implications for housing growth,

02:39:23.820 --> 02:39:27.420
economic development, and long-term infrastructure

02:39:27.900 --> 02:39:31.340
planning. An independent review is necessary

02:39:31.800 --> 02:39:35.760
to determine how this situation developed and why

02:39:36.260 --> 02:39:40.120
early warning signs did not lead to earlier action or

02:39:40.280 --> 02:39:42.440
clearer reporting to council.

02:39:43.400 --> 02:39:46.960
A review conducted by external experts provides

02:39:47.460 --> 02:39:50.880
credibility and objectivity. It allows council

02:39:51.380 --> 02:39:56.280
and the public to be confident that the issue is being examined

02:39:56.780 --> 02:40:00.690
thoroughly and without institutional bias. The goal

02:40:01.190 --> 02:40:04.730
is not to assign blame, and I want to emphasize that, but to

02:40:05.230 --> 02:40:08.570
identify weaknesses in forecasting, monitoring,

02:40:09.070 --> 02:40:12.610
and reporting so that future infrastructure challenges

02:40:12.929 --> 02:40:16.370
are identified earlier and managed more

02:40:16.870 --> 02:40:20.210
effectively. Regarding staff workload,

02:40:20.530 --> 02:40:24.650
a properly structured independent review will not interfere

02:40:25.150 --> 02:40:29.160
with staff's efforts to address the water supply challenge.

02:40:29.320 --> 02:40:32.360
And that's something we're all focused on, and I get that.

02:40:34.680 --> 02:40:39.080
In public sector investigations, the majority of the analytical

02:40:39.580 --> 02:40:43.320
work is carried out by the external reviewers themselves.

02:40:44.040 --> 02:40:47.960
External investigations typically rely heavily on

02:40:48.460 --> 02:40:51.760
existing reports, modelling data, and technical

02:40:52.260 --> 02:40:55.160
documentation that staff have already produced.

02:40:57.640 --> 02:41:01.120
Staff participation is usually limited to a

02:41:01.620 --> 02:41:05.160
small number of scheduled interviews or clarification meetings

02:41:05.880 --> 02:41:09.640
that are planned in advance. This approach ensures

02:41:10.140 --> 02:41:13.880
that staff can continue focusing on their primary responsibility,

02:41:14.760 --> 02:41:18.080
improving water supply and addressing the capacity

02:41:18.580 --> 02:41:22.640
shortfall. Which independent expert, while independent experts

02:41:22.880 --> 02:41:26.720
examined how the situation developed. In many cases,

02:41:27.200 --> 02:41:30.600
independent reviews also reduce pressure on

02:41:31.100 --> 02:41:34.440
staff by shifting the responsibility for examining

02:41:34.940 --> 02:41:38.320
the past decisions and system failures to an

02:41:38.820 --> 02:41:43.120
external body. Independent reviews are common practice

02:41:44.160 --> 02:41:47.640
when major operational or instructional challenges

02:41:48.140 --> 02:41:51.720
arise. Municipal governments, hospital systems

02:41:52.220 --> 02:41:56.400
and provincial agencies frequently commission external

02:41:56.900 --> 02:42:01.080
reviews following system failures and planning breakdowns.

02:42:01.480 --> 02:42:04.200
These reviews bring technical expertise,

02:42:04.760 --> 02:42:07.400
independence and public credibility.

02:42:11.160 --> 02:42:15.000
There is a long-standing practice in

02:42:15.500 --> 02:42:19.800
Ontario of commissioning independent reviews after major public system

02:42:19.880 --> 02:42:24.200
failures in order to restore public confidence and

02:42:24.920 --> 02:42:27.720
identify systemic weaknesses.

02:42:28.680 --> 02:42:32.120
After the Walkerton tragedy in 2000, the province

02:42:32.620 --> 02:42:36.360
established the Walkerton Inquiry to examine failures

02:42:36.860 --> 02:42:40.920
in testing, oversight and reporting with the municipal water system.

02:42:41.830 --> 02:42:45.830
Following repeated derailments and operational problems

02:42:45.990 --> 02:42:49.510
with Ottawa's Confederation Line LRT,

02:42:49.830 --> 02:42:53.430
a commission launched into the failures of the Ottawa Light

02:42:53.930 --> 02:42:58.710
Rail Transit system with a public inquiry in 2022.

02:43:02.950 --> 02:43:07.680
After the 2012 collapse of the Algoma Algonquin,

02:43:07.840 --> 02:43:11.680
Centre Mowat and Elliot Lake, Ontario Commissioned

02:43:11.760 --> 02:43:14.640
to look into what were the structural failures.

02:43:15.280 --> 02:43:19.840
Ontario hospitals also have had commissioned external

02:43:20.340 --> 02:43:24.000
reviews in pediatric forensic pathology at Toronto

02:43:24.240 --> 02:43:27.760
Hospital for Sick Children and

02:43:28.260 --> 02:43:32.000
independent reviews at Niagara Health and Windsor Regional

02:43:32.500 --> 02:43:35.590
Hospitals. So these are just examples of reviews

02:43:35.750 --> 02:43:39.150
that are done and they're done in parallel with the

02:43:39.650 --> 02:43:42.950
existing staff. They're not overwhelming them,

02:43:43.450 --> 02:43:46.790
they're not doing a number of those things that we are concerned about.

02:43:47.110 --> 02:43:52.350
And they have been successful in outlining the

02:43:52.850 --> 02:43:56.390
issues that took place and making recommendation. So the

02:43:56.890 --> 02:44:00.640
consequences of not doing a review. If the review

02:44:00.800 --> 02:44:04.360
region does not examine how this water capacity crisis

02:44:04.860 --> 02:44:08.440
developed, several risks remain. Loss of

02:44:08.940 --> 02:44:11.680
public confidence in regional infrastructure planning,

02:44:12.160 --> 02:44:14.480
unresolved governance issues.

02:44:16.320 --> 02:44:19.880
If council does not understand fully why

02:44:20.380 --> 02:44:24.160
the warning signals were not communicated, economic and

02:44:24.660 --> 02:44:28.650
housing impacts as water constraints affect development approvals.

02:44:29.530 --> 02:44:33.530
An independent review is a responsible and necessary step.

02:44:34.010 --> 02:44:38.330
It will provide transparency, strengthen public confidence,

02:44:38.570 --> 02:44:42.010
and ensure that the region of Waterloo learns

02:44:42.510 --> 02:44:46.370
from this infrastructure failure. Most importantly, it will

02:44:46.870 --> 02:44:50.410
produce recommendations for the future that will help Council

02:44:50.570 --> 02:44:54.440
ensure that the critical infrastructure risks are identified

02:44:55.080 --> 02:44:58.640
earlier and managed more effectively in the future. Thank you,

02:44:59.140 --> 02:45:02.480
Madam Chair. Thank you, I'm gonna go to Councillor James as

02:45:02.980 --> 02:45:06.040
a seconder and then with everyone's indulgence, I'm gonna go to Councillor Vrbanovic

02:45:06.540 --> 02:45:09.319
because he has a conflict shortly. Thank you through you,

02:45:09.320 --> 02:45:12.680
Chair, and I wanna speak to the support,

02:45:13.000 --> 02:45:16.480
to this motion in support of the intent

02:45:16.980 --> 02:45:20.330
of this motion. Councillor Craig, I'm gonna read as well, so I could

02:45:20.830 --> 02:45:24.410
try and stay on script. I support this motion. This is

02:45:24.570 --> 02:45:27.530
one of the most important responsibilities we have as a region,

02:45:27.850 --> 02:45:31.130
that our residents, businesses, local municipalities, they depend on

02:45:31.630 --> 02:45:35.890
reliable and transparent information about capacity to make long-term

02:45:36.390 --> 02:45:40.130
decisions. So as chair of the committee that

02:45:40.630 --> 02:45:44.010
this technically falls under, that has been chairing these committees

02:45:44.510 --> 02:45:48.090
until we've created the special committee for this, which was needed,

02:45:48.980 --> 02:45:52.380
I've had a lot of time to listen, actively listen to the

02:45:52.880 --> 02:45:56.300
discussions, heard directly from members of the public. And I'm

02:45:56.800 --> 02:46:00.700
not just talking developers, I'm talking about, you know, people who are concerned

02:46:01.200 --> 02:46:04.820
about water, you know, regular everyday residents who are

02:46:05.320 --> 02:46:08.940
concerned, who want clearer understanding of what happened

02:46:09.440 --> 02:46:12.740
and how we move forward. And that interest from the community reflects the

02:46:13.240 --> 02:46:17.110
importance of of transparency and maintaining public confidence in our

02:46:17.610 --> 02:46:21.390
processes. So, you know, when the questions about projections

02:46:21.890 --> 02:46:25.870
and communication or communication come up, it is responsible

02:46:26.370 --> 02:46:30.350
for Council to seek clearer understanding of process. An independent review

02:46:30.850 --> 02:46:34.430
can help strengthen government governance, improve reporting systems, and ensure

02:46:34.930 --> 02:46:38.190
that Council receives timely information in the future. For me,

02:46:38.690 --> 02:46:42.400
the focus should be on learning and improving systems, not assigning

02:46:42.900 --> 02:46:46.280
blame. That is not what a review is about. I think we need answers,

02:46:46.780 --> 02:46:50.640
and I think there's an importance in understanding the

02:46:51.140 --> 02:46:54.560
past to make sure that going forward in the future that we do not incur

02:46:55.060 --> 02:46:58.440
or future councils do not have the same situation.

02:46:58.680 --> 02:47:02.480
And I understand that staff operate with complex processes,

02:47:02.980 --> 02:47:06.720
and when challenges arise, it is often the reporting structures escalating

02:47:07.220 --> 02:47:10.720
protocols, or government governance frameworks that need to be reviewed

02:47:11.220 --> 02:47:15.040
and strengthened. So with that in mind, I would like to, I do

02:47:15.540 --> 02:47:18.760
support this motion. I do have one amendment,

02:47:19.260 --> 02:47:22.640
Councillor Craig, and that is regarding the time. I know you have six

02:47:23.140 --> 02:47:26.480
months on here. I would like to make sure that this is done in

02:47:26.980 --> 02:47:30.760
a comprehensive manner that isn't rushed. So I would

02:47:31.260 --> 02:47:35.940
like to suggest between nine and 12 months. Months for this to come back for

02:47:36.440 --> 02:47:39.580
review. Councillor Craig,

02:47:40.080 --> 02:47:43.500
are you amenable? Of course I am. Okay. And with that,

02:47:44.000 --> 02:47:47.340
I will conclude my remarks. I do hope, Council, I know there'll be discussion around

02:47:47.840 --> 02:47:51.300
this, but thinking about future councils, thinking about forward thinking growth,

02:47:51.540 --> 02:47:55.100
the impacts on this are not

02:47:55.600 --> 02:47:59.550
just on development community, because I think that's the pressing what

02:48:00.050 --> 02:48:03.470
we're hearing first and foremost, but also on the greater economic stability

02:48:03.970 --> 02:48:07.710
of this region. So it is critical we do our part as governance,

02:48:08.210 --> 02:48:11.830
as the board of governors for this region, to make sure that we do

02:48:12.330 --> 02:48:17.150
our part in ensuring this is not something that future councils have to endure.

02:48:17.230 --> 02:48:21.070
Thank you. So the mover and the seconder are

02:48:21.570 --> 02:48:25.120
both agreeable to changing the timeframe to

02:48:25.620 --> 02:48:28.720
9 to 12 months. Do we have unanimous consent for that change?

02:48:31.040 --> 02:48:34.720
Okay, I see no objections, so that will be unanimously

02:48:36.000 --> 02:48:38.400
approved. Councillor Vrbanovic.

02:48:39.200 --> 02:48:43.440
Thank you very much, Chair Redman and thank you to Councillor

02:48:44.320 --> 02:48:47.520
Craig for bringing this motion forward.

02:48:48.720 --> 02:48:52.560
I know we don't need it, but I'd be happy to third it. Listen,

02:48:53.360 --> 02:48:57.440
I believe that this is a

02:48:57.940 --> 02:49:01.200
critical action for this council to take.

02:49:01.360 --> 02:49:04.680
And I say that because as I reflect back on my

02:49:05.180 --> 02:49:08.600
time on regional council or even reflecting my

02:49:09.100 --> 02:49:13.120
history in local government in general, this is, as I've said before, the single

02:49:13.620 --> 02:49:17.520
biggest issue in terms of its overall implications.

02:49:18.320 --> 02:49:22.920
On the community that I can recall in

02:49:23.420 --> 02:49:26.960
my time. And I think this motion is

02:49:27.040 --> 02:49:30.360
very important because it's critical for

02:49:30.860 --> 02:49:34.480
us to fully understand where we've come from, we're working

02:49:34.560 --> 02:49:37.760
now on where we are, and we're also working on where we're going.

02:49:38.080 --> 02:49:42.160
But as we know, history repeats itself if you don't understand where

02:49:42.660 --> 02:49:46.480
you've come from. And I think this motion that Councillor Craig has brought forward is

02:49:46.780 --> 02:49:49.980
really trying to help us understand where we've come from.

02:49:50.460 --> 02:49:53.820
And it really does, in my view, three key things.

02:49:54.940 --> 02:49:58.180
It's focused on trust, it's focusing on learning,

02:49:58.680 --> 02:50:01.660
and it's focusing on acting. And when I speak about trust,

02:50:02.459 --> 02:50:05.540
it's really working to ensure that there's

02:50:06.040 --> 02:50:09.940
transparency to understanding how we got here. Listen, I mean,

02:50:10.440 --> 02:50:13.700
all of us know that for years we we received the drinking water

02:50:14.200 --> 02:50:18.300
summary report. None of these issues were flagged. We know that

02:50:18.800 --> 02:50:22.540
we were talking about being a million ready and constructing more homes.

02:50:23.040 --> 02:50:26.500
And then in the, you know, in, in the, the, the, the,

02:50:27.000 --> 02:50:29.900
the final weeks of 2025,

02:50:30.220 --> 02:50:33.500
all of a sudden, the world changed and

02:50:34.620 --> 02:50:37.980
there was new information and we had to go in a different direction.

02:50:38.510 --> 02:50:41.710
And so I think it's important from a transparency point of

02:50:42.210 --> 02:50:46.350
view and from the perspective of restoring confidence in

02:50:46.850 --> 02:50:50.390
our residents in general, but also in terms of the business community and

02:50:50.890 --> 02:50:54.309
the investor community that we embark on this process. And I will

02:50:54.809 --> 02:50:58.270
agree that this is an issue that we're hearing from all sorts of folks.

02:50:58.350 --> 02:51:01.710
I think in any community, two of the best

02:51:02.210 --> 02:51:05.700
places to find out what's happening is go to the grocery store and

02:51:06.200 --> 02:51:09.580
talk to people and or ride in a taxi.

02:51:10.080 --> 02:51:13.580
And I will tell you being at the grocery store last weekend, this came up

02:51:14.080 --> 02:51:17.860
both from staff and everyday citizens at the grocery store who were asking me

02:51:18.360 --> 02:51:21.860
about it. Secondly, on the learning piece, this is

02:51:22.360 --> 02:51:26.380
gonna help us get to the points of how, what did we know when,

02:51:27.820 --> 02:51:31.640
why didn't we take the decisions that staff did? In the

02:51:32.140 --> 02:51:35.680
past and then ultimately it'll help us

02:51:35.840 --> 02:51:39.200
with the ensuring that we act going forward

02:51:39.700 --> 02:51:44.160
in terms of next steps. This is really in my mind a

02:51:44.660 --> 02:51:48.080
tool to help everyone including the staff team that we have in

02:51:48.580 --> 02:51:52.320
place do a more effective job and

02:51:52.820 --> 02:51:56.400
I think as Councillor Craig outlined it it can be done in a way

02:51:57.080 --> 02:52:00.600
and I expect it to be done in a way that it has little impact

02:52:00.760 --> 02:52:04.640
on day-to-day business because the focus of our staff really needs to

02:52:05.140 --> 02:52:08.560
be on the solutions going forward. So thank you

02:52:09.060 --> 02:52:12.520
again, Councillor Craig, for moving in, Councillor James,

02:52:13.020 --> 02:52:16.840
for seconding it, and I'm happy to support it. So thank you, Councillor Vrbanovic.

02:52:17.340 --> 02:52:21.080
And we don't take thirds for motions, but it's duly noted you're fully

02:52:21.580 --> 02:52:24.980
in support. So if you get the way we understand that you are supportive.

02:52:25.540 --> 02:52:29.260
Councillor Huinik. Thank you to Councillor Craig for

02:52:29.760 --> 02:52:33.340
bringing this forward and thank you to Councillor

02:52:33.840 --> 02:52:37.740
James for seconding it and Councillor Vrbanovic for outlining the

02:52:38.240 --> 02:52:41.140
trust building in the community. I do think that's really, really important.

02:52:42.100 --> 02:52:45.980
I have one concern that I need to lay to rest before I decide to

02:52:46.480 --> 02:52:49.890
support this wholeheartedly and that is that we've been told time

02:52:50.390 --> 02:52:53.650
and time and time again by every expert and person that sat

02:52:54.150 --> 02:52:58.170
around the table talking about the water issue that our water system

02:52:58.410 --> 02:53:02.570
is very unique. That is why the provincial monitoring

02:53:03.070 --> 02:53:06.250
system did not catch the issues earlier, I think,

02:53:07.130 --> 02:53:09.930
or what I've understood, stood up until this point.

02:53:11.370 --> 02:53:14.650
So my worry in hiring an independent

02:53:15.150 --> 02:53:19.070
reviewer is how do we ensure that that independent reviewer

02:53:19.570 --> 02:53:22.830
actually has more expertise than we've already

02:53:23.330 --> 02:53:27.230
heard from? Because if they unfortunately have

02:53:27.550 --> 02:53:31.190
less expertise, that could lead to bad

02:53:31.690 --> 02:53:35.830
information that further complicates the matter and messaging

02:53:36.330 --> 02:53:36.510
to the community.

02:53:42.280 --> 02:53:45.720
So who would like to take that one? Mathieu.

02:53:47.400 --> 02:53:49.720
To you, Chair, I can take that one at a,

02:53:51.800 --> 02:53:55.800
maybe at a high level. I think we're looking for different kind

02:53:56.300 --> 02:54:00.080
of expertise. I think the focus there, and I know the team has

02:54:00.580 --> 02:54:04.440
been really thinking about and reading the details

02:54:04.940 --> 02:54:08.690
of the motion, really thinking about what What are the reporting mechanisms?

02:54:09.190 --> 02:54:10.930
What are the triggers for escalation? What information,

02:54:12.290 --> 02:54:15.650
because you've heard about a lot of information on water that goes to

02:54:16.150 --> 02:54:19.690
the ministry, and a lot of it is highly technical. We don't

02:54:20.190 --> 02:54:23.730
bring that back to council historically. So I think reviewing it from a process

02:54:23.810 --> 02:54:27.410
standpoint requires a bit of a different

02:54:27.490 --> 02:54:30.570
kind of skill set. It's less of

02:54:31.070 --> 02:54:34.630
a technical one, but more of a process and reporting review,

02:54:35.030 --> 02:54:39.070
understanding, and to your point, still with the understanding

02:54:39.570 --> 02:54:42.470
of the specific risks of our system, because as we understand,

02:54:42.870 --> 02:54:46.550
the methodology change that was brought forward in order

02:54:47.050 --> 02:54:50.710
to reflect the specific way in which our

02:54:51.510 --> 02:54:54.870
system operates and its specific vulnerabilities,

02:54:55.590 --> 02:54:59.030
but I think the process piece will be very important.

02:54:59.470 --> 02:55:03.550
And it will be time-- it will

02:55:04.050 --> 02:55:08.430
take time from staff to be able to inform on

02:55:08.510 --> 02:55:11.710
how the system works and what its vulnerability might be,

02:55:12.210 --> 02:55:15.710
what its strengths are. But it will be time well

02:55:16.210 --> 02:55:20.390
spent because I think that will help us to really make a more robust

02:55:20.890 --> 02:55:24.990
reporting process and clarify your role as the system owner

02:55:25.490 --> 02:55:28.340
in there and the information that you need to have as the owner of the

02:55:28.840 --> 02:55:31.820
system to be able to make these long lasting decisions.

02:55:32.300 --> 02:55:36.140
So thank you, Mathieu, for that answer.

02:55:36.860 --> 02:55:40.580
I think because I am in favor of a second opinion

02:55:41.080 --> 02:55:44.300
and because this is a bigger issue than this council has ever dealt with,

02:55:44.780 --> 02:55:48.140
I will support the motion with my concerns noted.

02:55:48.640 --> 02:55:52.100
I think for me, though, to be at rest, it'll be important for the

02:55:52.600 --> 02:55:57.060
expertise of whichever independent reviewers we get to

02:55:57.560 --> 02:56:02.420
be well understood by council and to know how seriously

02:56:02.920 --> 02:56:06.060
to take their implications. And quite honestly, the fact

02:56:06.560 --> 02:56:10.700
that Mr. Brothers has only been here for 12 days feels

02:56:11.200 --> 02:56:14.540
like an independent review, but I realise that's not how

02:56:15.040 --> 02:56:17.060
it's perceived from an external perspective.

02:56:18.500 --> 02:56:21.350
So I will Support the motion, thanks.

02:56:22.630 --> 02:56:25.990
Thank you for that, Councillor Hinink, and thank you for the endorsement,

02:56:26.490 --> 02:56:28.550
which I think we all share of Commissioner Brothers.

02:56:30.070 --> 02:56:33.350
Councillor Wolf. Through you, Madam Chair.

02:56:35.189 --> 02:56:38.230
Originally, I was not keen on supporting this,

02:56:39.110 --> 02:56:42.790
but after hearing from Councillor

02:56:42.870 --> 02:56:46.230
James, and that it's nine to 12 months,

02:56:46.860 --> 02:56:50.500
I feel the timing is much better in

02:56:51.000 --> 02:56:54.380
terms of, I think we've had so many motions where we're asking

02:56:54.880 --> 02:56:58.460
for information immediately. And I think

02:56:58.960 --> 02:57:02.660
that does put too much pressure on staff. So the fact that we're

02:57:03.160 --> 02:57:06.100
looking at a 9 to 12 month window, I think,

02:57:06.600 --> 02:57:10.340
takes pressure off staff and will

02:57:10.840 --> 02:57:14.020
lead to a more fulsome report. And I think

02:57:14.520 --> 02:57:18.100
that it'll be the new council that gets that report. And between

02:57:18.180 --> 02:57:19.380
staff and the new council,

02:57:21.220 --> 02:57:25.380
hopefully will provide a good tool to

02:57:25.880 --> 02:57:29.500
make our process better. I do have a

02:57:30.000 --> 02:57:33.140
question though, and that is how much will

02:57:33.640 --> 02:57:37.340
this cost? Normally when we have a motion where there's

02:57:37.840 --> 02:57:42.270
a cost of associated with it, that information

02:57:42.430 --> 02:57:46.070
is given to us. So I do know that these

02:57:46.570 --> 02:57:50.590
things can be expensive. So I wonder if staff

02:57:51.090 --> 02:57:55.790
has any projection on how much a review would

02:57:56.290 --> 02:57:58.670
cost. Commissioner Steffler is happy to jump in.

02:58:01.310 --> 02:58:05.450
Yeah, through the chair. So I think To

02:58:05.950 --> 02:58:09.210
really get at this, we would go through our normal procurement process where

02:58:09.710 --> 02:58:14.370
we would scope out and try to identify what the work activities

02:58:14.870 --> 02:58:19.290
would be to do this. So it's a little difficult to estimate

02:58:19.790 --> 02:58:21.690
that. I could ballpark,

02:58:23.610 --> 02:58:26.890
maybe in the 50,000 range,

02:58:27.390 --> 02:58:30.610
but it's really difficult until we do a bit of an

02:58:31.110 --> 02:58:34.610
assessment to see what the scope of it will be, what the work activities would

02:58:35.040 --> 02:58:38.000
and then we would be able to go through the procurement process.

02:58:38.080 --> 02:58:42.240
I was concerned because we spent $50,000 on

02:58:42.720 --> 02:58:45.760
the consultant that reviewed our salaries,

02:58:46.000 --> 02:58:48.960
which was maybe a three-week process.

02:58:49.040 --> 02:58:53.200
I don't know, it wasn't that extensive. So if

02:58:53.700 --> 02:58:57.400
we're looking at this, it seems

02:58:57.900 --> 02:59:01.160
much more so, Mr. Steffler, is it fair to assume

02:59:01.660 --> 02:59:05.920
that whether there was an RFP or what those terms

02:59:06.420 --> 02:59:10.320
of engagement would be that they could come back and close

02:59:10.820 --> 02:59:14.320
to council for council review before we sign off? Yeah, sure.

02:59:14.920 --> 02:59:18.440
We could scope this out a bit more and identify what it would be.

02:59:18.940 --> 02:59:23.480
We could go through and review some of the applicants

02:59:23.980 --> 02:59:27.440
that we get that are interested in it and deal

02:59:27.940 --> 02:59:31.340
with it that way. Would that satisfy your concerns? Thank you. Thank you.

02:59:31.420 --> 02:59:34.540
Councillor Shantz. Thank you.

02:59:34.860 --> 02:59:38.780
I support the motion for all the reasons that have already been

02:59:39.280 --> 02:59:42.700
stated. I'm not going to repeat them all. I do have sort

02:59:43.200 --> 02:59:48.340
of a question or maybe

02:59:48.840 --> 02:59:52.860
it's a concern and maybe it's not. And that is looking at just

02:59:53.360 --> 02:59:56.870
2021 to 2026. And I'd like to

02:59:56.950 --> 03:00:00.630
make sure, depending on what happens with the review,

03:00:00.790 --> 03:00:04.350
that there is the ability to go prior to

03:00:04.850 --> 03:00:08.070
2021 so that they're not restricted to

03:00:08.570 --> 03:00:09.830
this timeframe.

03:00:11.590 --> 03:00:15.090
I'm not sure if that needs to be an

03:00:15.590 --> 03:00:18.630
Is that something we could bring back? I guess I'm looking at Steph.

03:00:19.270 --> 03:00:22.790
Amy, do you want to comment? Does that seem like a reasonable timeframe to you?

03:00:24.840 --> 03:00:28.280
So through the chair, I don't know how that date was chosen.

03:00:28.680 --> 03:00:32.320
The only thing that may come up is around the 2015 water

03:00:32.820 --> 03:00:36.320
supply strategy master plan. Like there could be some components around that that

03:00:36.820 --> 03:00:40.320
will feed into some of the history. But again, I'm not

03:00:40.820 --> 03:00:43.000
sure on the rationale for the 2021. I don't think that's a problem.

03:00:44.120 --> 03:00:47.480
Councillor Craig, did you have rationale while you chose that as a start date?

03:00:49.030 --> 03:00:51.110
Well, I always have rationale, Madam Chair.

03:00:52.630 --> 03:00:56.270
You know, I've never done a review like this before, even suggested

03:00:56.770 --> 03:01:00.110
it. So really, I'm putting out kind of a bare bones kind of issue in

03:01:00.610 --> 03:01:03.710
terms of how we look at it. I would expect staff to

03:01:04.210 --> 03:01:06.710
come back and say, well, maybe this should be broader.

03:01:07.190 --> 03:01:10.670
This is the cost. That's what I would expect. I mean,

03:01:11.170 --> 03:01:14.910
today, really, I think hopefully we're moving forward to say, okay, we're going to

03:01:15.410 --> 03:01:17.630
do it. And then we can sort it out, okay?

03:01:18.430 --> 03:01:21.630
So I think with that explicit explanation,

03:01:22.130 --> 03:01:25.350
Councillor Shantz, we would ask staff to come back and comment if they thought the

03:01:25.850 --> 03:01:28.830
2015 master water plan should be part of this.

03:01:30.830 --> 03:01:34.030
I think where I'm going with this is we're asking a third party

03:01:34.530 --> 03:01:38.390
to come in and do a review and so the

03:01:38.890 --> 03:01:42.430
first thing it says when capacity concerns were first identified.

03:01:42.830 --> 03:01:46.670
So if they're looking at it and find out that while

03:01:47.170 --> 03:01:51.150
there was something that was identified in 2018 that we don't say,

03:01:51.650 --> 03:01:55.710
I'm sorry, you're only looking at 2021 to 2026.

03:01:58.030 --> 03:02:01.470
That, and so, yeah, I mean, our staff could do that. I don't

03:02:01.970 --> 03:02:04.830
think I need to create more work for our staff. I just want to ensure

03:02:05.330 --> 03:02:08.890
the external consultants when they're looking at it have

03:02:09.390 --> 03:02:13.370
the capacity to, if they feel it needs to be, to go outside

03:02:13.450 --> 03:02:15.850
those years. Ken's prepared to weigh in.

03:02:17.050 --> 03:02:19.050
Thank you, Chair.

03:02:21.610 --> 03:02:26.130
I think by scoping out what the issue is and doing investigation

03:02:26.630 --> 03:02:30.610
in terms of what transpired when, if it takes us back to that particular date,

03:02:31.110 --> 03:02:34.090
then I think the consultants should explore that. I mean,

03:02:34.250 --> 03:02:38.650
it's a trail, it's an investigation, and you follow the lead and

03:02:39.150 --> 03:02:42.410
investigate that to have a complete comprehensive assessment.

03:02:42.970 --> 03:02:46.890
So I think this should be perhaps captured in the request

03:02:47.390 --> 03:02:51.370
for proposals in terms of sketching out. We're looking at the history here. It may

03:02:51.450 --> 03:02:55.290
bring you back a number of years back to previous strategic plans,

03:02:55.610 --> 03:02:59.130
but I wouldn't suggest that we cap it in time.

03:02:59.630 --> 03:03:02.890
I think we set a framework that allows investigation to proceed.

03:03:03.620 --> 03:03:06.420
And having said that, that's my view.

03:03:07.780 --> 03:03:10.420
In terms of the cost,

03:03:11.060 --> 03:03:14.460
as we're talking now, extended period of time of nine months and

03:03:14.960 --> 03:03:18.620
so on, that will generate budget

03:03:19.120 --> 03:03:22.660
demands. So in as much as Councillor Steffler

03:03:23.160 --> 03:03:24.980
and I had some previous discussions on cost,

03:03:26.580 --> 03:03:30.260
I would expect it to be significantly more than the $50,000.

03:03:31.060 --> 03:03:34.100
Based upon the track of discussion we're having here.

03:03:34.820 --> 03:03:38.340
So Councillor Shantz, so do I need to make an amendment

03:03:38.840 --> 03:03:43.060
to remove the 2021 and say prior to 2026?

03:03:43.860 --> 03:03:47.420
Does that have to go as an amendment or how

03:03:47.920 --> 03:03:51.020
would I handle that? If it

03:03:51.520 --> 03:03:54.100
did, I would second it. I'm wondering if,

03:03:55.060 --> 03:03:56.980
hang on a minute, we're gonna confer.

03:04:09.670 --> 03:04:12.990
Kim's gonna help us. So through the chair,

03:04:13.490 --> 03:04:17.830
I think either approach would be appropriate. It could be an amendment or

03:04:17.990 --> 03:04:21.150
the CAO could take it under advisement that it not be

03:04:21.650 --> 03:04:25.960
limited to 2021. Through the appointment

03:04:26.360 --> 03:04:29.520
process. So I would make an

03:04:30.020 --> 03:04:34.360
amendment that we change it from 2021

03:04:34.860 --> 03:04:38.040
to 2026 to prior to 2026.

03:04:39.800 --> 03:04:44.360
Okay, so that's moved by Councillor Shantz, seconded by Councillor Huinik, any conversation

03:04:44.860 --> 03:04:46.200
on that amendment? Councillor Erb?

03:04:52.130 --> 03:04:55.570
Okay, so I was going to suggest the amendment

03:04:56.070 --> 03:04:58.850
if Councillor Shantz did not, so that's why I'm on the list. So I can

03:04:59.350 --> 03:05:02.690
