haven't supported many of his motions in the last month or two, so we're

03:06:04.580 --> 03:06:08.520
friends again. I I hope we're not setting any.

03:06:09.830 --> 03:06:13.830
Expectations up in the broader community or around the council

03:06:13.910 --> 03:06:17.550
table for this council or future councils that this study

03:06:18.050 --> 03:06:22.470
is going to show some yah-ha moment that all of a sudden something

03:06:22.970 --> 03:06:26.750
happened. Because I think with our complicated water system and what I've been able

03:06:27.250 --> 03:06:30.990
to learn from staff that there's

03:06:31.490 --> 03:06:35.260
been these indicators over the last two or three years and it hasn't

03:06:35.760 --> 03:06:38.260
been this one thing. There's been a number of things over the last two or

03:06:38.760 --> 03:06:42.340
three years that have brought us to where we are today. And so I'm grateful

03:06:42.420 --> 03:06:45.580
to staff and for the monitoring that they've been doing that they brought

03:06:46.080 --> 03:06:49.660
this to us before it's a crisis situation and that we were able

03:06:50.160 --> 03:06:54.060
to deal with it now. We're dealing with

03:06:54.560 --> 03:06:58.140
climate change, but it wasn't a week or two that we realised we

03:06:58.640 --> 03:07:02.100
had a climate change issue. It evolved over a certain length of time and and

03:07:03.780 --> 03:07:07.340
we learned that certain foods aren't good for us and it took years for

03:07:07.840 --> 03:07:11.180
us to figure that out. And so I think the issue that

03:07:11.680 --> 03:07:14.780
we're dealing with at the region right now is something that evolved over two or

03:07:15.280 --> 03:07:18.620
three years that our staff had been monitoring and all of a sudden

03:07:19.120 --> 03:07:21.140
there was a couple of lights that went on that said we need to bring

03:07:21.640 --> 03:07:24.900
some attention to this. And so I'm grateful for that to happen and I'm grateful

03:07:25.400 --> 03:07:29.030
to support the motion that we can create some kind of a

03:07:29.530 --> 03:07:32.790
confidence in the community as to where we're at

03:07:33.290 --> 03:07:36.710
with this system. Remembering that we've been told we have

03:07:37.210 --> 03:07:40.950
one of the most complicated water systems in the country. So colleagues,

03:07:41.450 --> 03:07:44.430
I have no further speakers, so I'm going to ask you to cast your ballot

03:07:45.470 --> 03:07:46.670
on eScribe.

03:08:22.290 --> 03:08:25.490
so I'll mark Councillor Vrbanovic as absent, although he did

03:08:25.990 --> 03:08:29.290
indicate his enthusiasm to support this and it is carried,

03:08:29.790 --> 03:08:33.730
colleagues. The next notice of motion is from Councillor Gowing regarding

03:08:33.970 --> 03:08:37.410
permits to take water. Do you have a seconder for your motion?

03:08:38.290 --> 03:08:40.450
At the moment, I do not, but I'm looking for one.

03:08:41.410 --> 03:08:44.810
Councillor Wolf is willing to second it. Would you like to speak to the

03:08:45.310 --> 03:08:48.660
motion? Yes, thank you Chair. So I'm bringing this motion forward

03:08:48.820 --> 03:08:52.460
because of the groundwater capacity issues that we're seeing around

03:08:52.960 --> 03:08:56.540
the Mannheim service area. The province's own data shows that there's

03:08:57.040 --> 03:09:01.539
108 active water taking permits in Waterloo region allowing

03:09:02.039 --> 03:09:05.620
over 1 billion litres per day. Now that's not saying that we're meeting

03:09:06.120 --> 03:09:08.980
that target but it's eligible to hit that target.

03:09:09.780 --> 03:09:13.620
In the Mannheim in the Mannheim service area alone,

03:09:14.020 --> 03:09:18.140
there's 65 permits allowing up to 740

03:09:18.640 --> 03:09:22.420
million litres a day, including 268 million for private

03:09:22.920 --> 03:09:26.580
permit taking. This motion asks the province to pause new

03:09:27.080 --> 03:09:30.740
or expanding expanded private permits there

03:09:31.240 --> 03:09:34.860
until the water supply strategy update is complete and to ensure

03:09:35.360 --> 03:09:39.220
the region is properly notified and able to comment on applications.

03:09:39.540 --> 03:09:42.860
This is just about protecting the long-term sustainability of our

03:09:43.360 --> 03:09:46.100
groundwater, not to stop production.

03:09:49.380 --> 03:09:51.860
Councillor Wolfe, did you want to speak to it as a seconder? Sorry.

03:09:57.860 --> 03:10:01.660
Through Madam's chair. Just to say that I

03:10:02.160 --> 03:10:05.600
agree with Councillor Gowing and I think We actually

03:10:06.100 --> 03:10:09.040
had a delegate this morning, I think Matthew Parker,

03:10:09.200 --> 03:10:13.040
who spoke very well too about the

03:10:13.540 --> 03:10:16.840
fact that we should be monitoring the amount

03:10:17.340 --> 03:10:20.400
of water that the province is allowing

03:10:20.800 --> 03:10:24.880
to be taken out of our system. And I think by

03:10:25.380 --> 03:10:29.960
asking for a pause and for them to look at it more closely is

03:10:30.460 --> 03:10:33.090
something we need to do. Councillor James,

03:10:34.290 --> 03:10:37.250
thank you for bringing this motion forward. Councillor Gowing,

03:10:37.890 --> 03:10:41.010
sorry, through the chair. Thank you, Councillor Gowing,

03:10:41.510 --> 03:10:44.610
for bringing this motion forward. I do appreciate the intent of it.

03:10:44.690 --> 03:10:48.410
I agree with the intent of it. Again, I have some concerns that I

03:10:48.910 --> 03:10:52.250
need to lay to rest before I support it for the benefit of the

03:10:52.750 --> 03:10:55.970
community and everyone around this table in this room,

03:10:56.130 --> 03:10:59.530
etc. Et cetera, et cetera. The most shocking

03:11:00.030 --> 03:11:03.370
thing that occurred to me when I became a regional

03:11:03.870 --> 03:11:07.610
councillor was that the region and our partner municipalities,

03:11:07.850 --> 03:11:11.210
in fact, have a limited amount of autonomy.

03:11:11.290 --> 03:11:15.610
That means in many situations, we must collaborate

03:11:16.110 --> 03:11:19.890
with the province and we must, in fact, do what they

03:11:20.390 --> 03:11:23.660
instruct us to do. Therefore, I'm wondering

03:11:24.160 --> 03:11:27.900
