03:11:28.400 --> 03:11:32.060
Gowing's motion. And I'm also wondering, if in

03:11:32.560 --> 03:11:36.140
fact we need the province's support to fix the water

03:11:36.640 --> 03:11:40.100
system, which I think we will, will this

03:11:40.740 --> 03:11:44.500
motion be unduly prickly

03:11:44.820 --> 03:11:48.140
toward that relationship, even though the

03:11:48.640 --> 03:11:51.350
intent is positive and important and good.

03:11:54.870 --> 03:11:58.950
So is that a somewhat rhetorical question or would you like to ask

03:11:59.450 --> 03:12:03.630
staff maybe to outline the role that the province plays

03:12:04.130 --> 03:12:08.830
as well as the role that the region of Waterloo plays in this

03:12:09.330 --> 03:12:13.190
process as it now exists? I was hoping that someone could actually answer some of

03:12:13.690 --> 03:12:17.040
that, at least. Amy's willing to weigh in.

03:12:17.520 --> 03:12:21.520
So through the chair, I would say that we

03:12:22.020 --> 03:12:25.640
would continue as technical staff if they were to continue asking

03:12:26.140 --> 03:12:29.560
us for comments on permits to take water, if they did not take this

03:12:30.060 --> 03:12:34.160
recommendation, that we would continue to offer our technical comments

03:12:34.240 --> 03:12:37.520
based on a risk-based approach. That is how we're

03:12:38.020 --> 03:12:41.210
doing it now and we'll continue to do that if if asked to do so,

03:12:42.170 --> 03:12:45.290
looking after our water system. I do think,

03:12:45.610 --> 03:12:49.690
you know, the ministry may not appreciate us telling

03:12:50.190 --> 03:12:53.690
