03:12:58.190 --> 03:13:01.690
like that. But we'll continue to work with them on

03:13:02.190 --> 03:13:05.980
permit to take water applications that we ourselves have, because we also have for permit

03:13:06.480 --> 03:13:10.100
to take water applications. For some of these projects that are upcoming, we're also going

03:13:10.600 --> 03:13:13.180
to be seeking permit to take waters. So we have to be careful that we're

03:13:13.680 --> 03:13:17.380
not asking for a moratorium on permit to take waters when we're ourselves

03:13:17.880 --> 03:13:20.220
going to be asking for new permits to take waters.

03:13:21.500 --> 03:13:23.340
Jer, can I add two cents to that?

03:13:26.300 --> 03:13:29.660
Sure. Again, this is more so

03:13:30.160 --> 03:13:32.910
just an ask. We can't force the hand of the provincial government when it comes

03:13:33.410 --> 03:13:35.950
to comes to this, it is just an ask for them to look at the

03:13:36.450 --> 03:13:39.190
broader picture and look at the private sector,

03:13:39.350 --> 03:13:43.550
not the public sector, because we do need their assistance

03:13:44.050 --> 03:13:46.790
on this and approvals on future taking for us.

03:13:47.110 --> 03:13:50.430
It's more so, it's the sustainability on the

03:13:50.930 --> 03:13:53.190
private side, but this is just an ask. It's not,

03:13:54.310 --> 03:13:57.670
you need to do this. Council Hunic,

03:13:57.990 --> 03:14:01.120
thank you. Thank you, Councillor Gowing,

03:14:01.620 --> 03:14:05.480
